in this video we're gonna talk about how  to flush an hplc column in order to  maximize column life this is especially  important to do if you add buffers or  additives to your mobile phase for  instance most people use something like  ammonium acetate or formic acid etc over  time if the column isn't flushed out  regularly precipitates can form and it  can plug up your column thereby  destroying it we're going to show you  two techniques to extend your column  life as much as possible the first  method is your daily maintenance method  if you have a solenoid valve in your  pump you can select up to four solvents  a and b solvents can be used as your  standard mobile phases for regular  operations c and d then can be selected  and used as solvents for cleaning c d  would normally consist of water and some  kind of organic solvent like methanol  you can simply do a gradient after your  last run of five percent to 95 over an  hour and that should keep things nice  and clean if you don't have a solenoid  valve you're just gonna have to switch  the bottles if you feel like your column  needs a deeper cleaning it would be best  to do a reverse flush you start by  disconnecting the column at the low  pressure end and then the high pressure  end don't forget to remove the guard  lastly you flip the column around and  you can flow into a container so you  don't dirty your detector the method for  reverse flush would be to start with 95  percent water and 5  methanol for about 10 column volumes  then you do a gradient of 5 to 95  methanol for five column volumes and  lastly you hold five percent water and  95 methanol for 10 column volumes you  want to run this at half of your normal  flow rates for your method the way that  you know it's time to do a deeper  cleaning is to monitor your pressure  buildup on your column always note the  back pressure when you first install the  column so you have a baseline if you  notice your pressure kick up around 15  to 20 percent it's a good idea to do the  reverse flush that's it for the tutorial  today i hope that helps you keep your  column clean if you like this type of  content please like and subscribe it'll  really help us out a lot see you in the  next video
 

